# Build context exclusions. Everything here is either rebuilt inside the image
# or has no business in it.
#
# .git is the important one. Without it, "COPY . ." in the builder stage copies
# the entire repository history — 305MB and growing — into the image. That is
# what made GitHub-triggered builds take 8-10 minutes and then fail, while a
# CLI deploy (which excludes .git via .railwayignore) finished in 2.
.git
.github
node_modules
dist
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
.env
.env.*
npm-debug.log

# Not needed to build or run the server.
tests
docs
*.md
.claude
